 "limitations": [
  "Every observation is a subjective visual setting by one person on one clock, in the units of an integer slider. It is a preference, not a photometric measurement, and it is not transferable to another optical stack.",
  "Saturation is never interpolated from data: every colour observation is at sat=100 and every anchor at sat=0, so the linear fade between them is a declared assumption and nothing here tests it.",
  "The grid reproduces its own knots, so the in-sample numbers measure the drift correction and the integer quantisation and little else. Only the held-out folds say anything about a level nobody measured.",
  "Neither endpoint level can be cross-validated, so nothing here says what the profile is worth outside 0.02..10 lx, where it clamps.",
  "2 of 6 folds are unscored (0.02 lx, 10 lx): holding out the darkest level leaves every prediction clamped against it, which measures the clamp rather than the model; holding out the brightest level leaves every prediction clamped against it, which measures the clamp rather than the model.",
  "The measurements are not monotone in ambient light: white between 0.15 and 0.5 lx; hue 60 between 0.15 and 0.5 lx; hue 180 between 0.15 and 0.5 lx; hue 240 between 0.15 and 0.5 lx. The grid the evaluator reads has been projected onto the nearest non-decreasing one, which is a repair and not a measurement - the observed values are kept beside it.",
  "Hue 240 carries the whole shortfall: RMS 10.42 and worst 15 against 3.66 and 7 for every other hue together."
 ],
