  "families": [],
  "pairs": [],
  "residualNote": "A targeted pair measures one hue's residual a second time, so it joins that knot as a replicate and the knot becomes the mean of what it holds, weighted by how many observations that is. It fills in no other hue: a two-point sitting says nothing about the five it did not look at.",
  "validationOnly": [],
  "whiteBaseline": {
   "appliedTo": "residualsOnly",
   "ifPooled": [],
   "note": "A targeted pair's white anchor is used to normalise its own colour and nothing else. Its anchors sit up to half a decade below the six-hue rounds' at the dark levels, which says the session was in a different adaptation state rather than that the rounds were wrong - and one anchor from a session aimed at one hue must not move the baseline every hue is measured against. What it *would* have moved is reported under `ifPooled`, so the choice is evidence rather than assertion. The pair's same-sitting difference is unaffected by any of this, which is exactly why the residual travels and the level does not."
  }
